class::ErrorWrapper
summary:: Error used to wrap another error
categories::Core
related:: Classes/Error

description::
Used to wrap an existing error, providing more context through the code::what:: string while preserving the original backtrace.
It can be nested.


Here is an example using two functions code::f:: and code::g:: and a top level try that catches everything.

code::
(
var f = { |a| 
    if (a < 0 ) { 
        Error("Negative values are not allowed", [nil, "a negative value was passed here"]).throw
    } { 
        f.(a - 1)
    }
};

var g = { 
    try { f.(3) } { |e| ErrorWrapper(e, "Thrown while calling f").throw }
};

try { g.() } { |e| ErrorWrapper(e, "Thrown at top level").throw }
)
::

This produces a backtrace as follows.
code::
